(the `id = $3 AND id = $4` above is wrong on purpose to flag it — accounts is keyed by its own id, so really it's just `WHERE id = $3` where `$3` must *be* `req.user.accountId`, not `req.params.id`, since a user should only ever update their own account row: `"... WHERE id = $3", [..., req.user.accountId]`, dropping `req.params.id` entirely, or if `:id` is meant to support admins acting on other accounts, add a role check instead of trusting the param).

