Add an `Idempotency-Key` header + a unique constraint scoped to the account, then check-before-insert in `routes/orders.js:6-12`:

1. Schema: unique index on `orders (account_id, idempotency_key)` (nullable column, so it doesn't affect other write paths).
2. Handler: require the header, look up an existing row by `(account_id, idempotency_key)` before inserting; if found, return it instead of inserting again.
3. Race: two requests with the same key can both miss the lookup and both insert — catch the unique-violation (Postgres code `23505`) from `db.write` and re-fetch/return the existing row rather than erroring.

```js
